Subject: CPMS I03E3 Proof Oracle and Review Protocol Constraint Ledger

@ [ledger_uuid] 53452a76-f8ab-4b6e-a27e-074adc6e23cd
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cpms_i03e3_proof_oracle_review_protocol\Source_Document_Manifest.sop

& [E3C01] exact I03E I03E1 I03E2 case proposal and source identities bind review
& [E3C02] generator cannot authorize expectation
& [E3C03] implementation observation cannot define expectation
& [E3C04] comparator cannot rewrite expectation or observation
& [E3C05] admission cannot manufacture missing receipt or proof
& [E3C06] every expectation cites independent source rationale
& [E3C07] numeric and byte oracles use exact non-floating evidence
& [E3C08] semantic oracle uses independent vector derivation or proof identity
& [E3C09] authority oracle proves non-invocation and grants no semantic admission
& [E3C10] every case stage owns a separate expected disposition
& [E3C11] every CommonSyntaxClaim owns separately reviewed schema and typed witnesses
& [E3C12] every obligation edge is individually reviewable
& [E3C13] template similarity never creates root coverage
& [E3C14] Honesty and Security primary payloads contain no peer digest
& [E3C15] both cross acknowledgments bind both primary digests
& [E3C16] envelope binds two primaries two acknowledgments dispositions principals and independence class
& [E3C17] no digest field is included in its own digest payload
& [E3C18] content digest checksum attestation and digital signature remain distinct
& [E3C19] digital signatures require declared algorithm trusted key id and verification
& [E3C20] reviewer principal can be person or authorized provenance-bound faculty process
& [E3C21] raw model output alone has no review authority
& [E3C22] exact faculty SOP input output engine job and run identity bind automated review
& [E3C23] independence class is explicit and later minimum policy is not assumed
& [E3C24] dissent affirm challenge abstain and insufficient evidence are preserved
& [E3C25] open challenge abstention or insufficient evidence blocks affected admission
& [E3C26] dissent resolution creates successor and never deletes predecessor
& [E3C27] case content change invalidates prior case receipts
& [E3C28] expectation or mapping change creates receipt successor
& [E3C29] batch review lists every exact case and permits individual exceptions
& [E3C30] statistical sampling never admits unreviewed subjects
& [E3C31] faculty cycle outputs inspectable evidence not private chain-of-thought
& [E3C32] Observer verifies complete receipts cross confirmation dissent closure and accounts
& [E3C33] corpus_candidate_formed grants review status and no reader execution
& [E3C34] normative ordering and encoding exclude volatile values
& [E3C35] all receipt edge dissent batch reference and rationale counts are finite checked
& [E3C36] exhaustion leaves cases unreviewed and blocks admission
& [E3C37] no runtime file database cache network provider model service effect or hardware
& [E3C38] formation issues no receipt attestation key signature or corpus candidate
& [E3C39] later review catalogue requires new source preservation SJS trust policy and exact inventory
& [E3C40] execution requires separate satisfaction signature and active phase lock after review candidate formation

& [ConflictRule] a requirement violating E3C01 through E3C40 returns to SJS
& [LedgerDisposition] is closed_for_formation_not_review_execution
